<title>POLAND: Polish budget gap widens to PLN 6.58 bln in May.</title>
<headline>Polish budget gap widens to PLN 6.58 bln in May.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish budget deficit widened by 1.01 billion zlotys in May, bringing the shortfall in the January-May period to 6.58 billion zlotys, or 53.8 percent of the planned 1997 deficit, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p> POLISH BUDGET GAP   Jan-May	   Jan-April    1997 plan</p>
<p> balance in bln PLN	 6.579	     5.569	12.220</p>
<p> revenue		     40.713	    32.047     115.334</p>
<p> expenditure		 47.292	    37.616     127.554</p>
<p>NOTE: January-April figures given as reported last month.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
